  "title": "Krishnadevaraya",
  "summary": "Krishnadevaraya ruled the Vijayanagara empire from 1509 until his death, given as 1529 or 1530 depending on the source. EBSCO credits him with a system of subordinate chiefs, later called poligars, and with the Telugu epic poem Amuktamalyada. The Archaeological Survey of India says a large number of royal buildings at Hampi were raised by him, including the Pampapati temple entrance tower.",
